KZ3 patch 2147 (ENHANCEMENT, experimental): an opt-in FidelityFX Super Resolution 3.1 presentation filter.

The KZ3 build defines KZ3_FSR31 and supplies the port-owned fsr31.h adapter. Other ps3recomp users compile the
renderer unchanged. When requested, the renderer associates the primary display surface with its full-size depth
pass, applies SDK jitter only to eligible display-target 3D draws, snapshots the matching depth, and dispatches FSR
before scan-out gamma. Missing runtime/provider/camera/depth data, ambiguous views, unsupported dimensions, and
dispatch failures are logged and use the existing bilinear scaler instead.

This first experimental path deliberately supplies camera-rotation motion only. Translation, object motion,
reactive/transparency masks, and separate UI composition require further game-side evidence; the Options page
warns about ghosting and shimmer before enabling it. Output is capped at 3x the fixed render size, history resets
after gaps, target/context changes, and camera cuts, and resize recreation waits for prior GPU use to finish.

Host coverage: tools/smoke/test_display_mode.c (settings, persistence, confirmation UI) and the KZ3 adapter's
tools/smoke/test_fsr31.cpp / test_fsr31_motion.c probes.

Coexists with the upscaler interface of patch 2145: the display blit samples bilinearly whenever the filter is not
Nearest (its two sampling pipelines are indexed by that, not by the filter id, which for FSR 3.1 is 2). An FSR 3.1
image already has the rectangle's size, so an RSX_UPSCALE=fsr1 pass is not wanted then; on a Bilinear fallback
frame it runs as with any other filter. The settings comment keeps PS3RECOMP_PRODUCT_NAME (patch 2146).

